template:
DISPATCH TO: {agent}
MODE: checkpoint
SESSION DATE: {session_date}
SESSION ID: {session_id}
GENERATION: {generation}
BASELINE BRANCH: {baseline_branch}
HEAD SHA: {head_sha}
SCOPE: {scope}
RESULT KD: {result_kd}
KD PATHS: {kd_paths}

---

Load the kd-system skill. Load the committer-checkpoint skill. Read KDs from KD PATHS. The repository gates are verified green before this dispatch; the pre-commit hook runs them automatically at commit time. The commit payload is the code surface — tracked, non-gitignored changes; the impl KD plus the registry row are the scoring surface on disk. The checkpoint records the handoff whether or not a commit exists, and a knowledge-only handoff produces the record with no fabricated commit. Write a CHECKPOINT KD at {result_kd} using the `template-checkpoint` skill to signal completion.
